meta {
  name: 5.2.5 Generate slots
  type: http
  seq: 12
  tags: [
    write
    crud-schedules
    role-admin
  ]
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/schedules/{{newScheduleId}}/generate
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "from": "{{farFrom}}",
    "to": "{{farTo}}"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  if (!bru.getVar('newScheduleId')) { bru.runner.skipRequest(); }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.generated: isNumber
  res.body.skipped: isNumber
}

docs {
  Spec 5.2.5. ADMIN. Body `{ from, to }` (<= 90 days, calendar dates YYYY-MM-DD, inside the schedule's planning horizon: a day outside it -> 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`); 201 `{ generated, skipped }`, existing slots and slots that overlap an existing one are not written (counted in `skipped`); free slots of the schedule in the range that are not on the current grid are deleted first, busy ones are never touched. A run that wrote slots adds one `AuditEvent` (`create`, `Schedule/{id}`). Supports `Idempotency-Key` (UUID, 24 h): a repeat returns the cached answer, a repeat sent while the first request still runs -> 409 `CONFLICT`. 409 `CONFLICT` also for a deactivated schedule.
}
